<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Controller (VFEP v4.03,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Headgear.xml), its drone module left off; a field not
    discussed here is the Controller's. Plating, the research gate and the absent apparel
    tags follow the armor's header.

    Tuning: the set's answer to Biotech's mechlord helmet (MechBandwidth 12,
    ShootingAccuracyPawn -5, MeleeHitChance -0.5; Plasteel 120, ComponentSpacer 6,
    NanostructuringChip 2), on the tier's plating and vacuum seal.
    - MechBandwidth 12, the mechlord helmet's.
    - ShootingAccuracyPawn -3 and no MeleeHitChance: three fifths of vanilla's shooting price
      and none of its melee one, because a warcasket pilot still fights at the front where
      the mechlord pair (-10 shooting, -1 melee) makes a commander who does not. The offset
      is skill levels added before the stat's curve, not a percentage: the pilot shoots as
      if three Shooting levels lower.
    - No PsychicSensitivity offset, where the Controller's helmet has -0.5. With the armor's
      -0.5 that would leave a baseline pilot at zero, and CompUseEffect_InstallImplant refuses
      a mechlink (requiresPsychicallySensitive) to a pawn at zero.
    - costList: ComponentSpacer 6 is the mechlord helmet's. Of its two NanostructuringChips
      one is traded for the war queen's PowerfocusChip, the chip Biotech's integrator headset
      pays for its bandwidth; the trade keeps the set from asking the apocriton four times
      (the armor's header has the set's count). Plasteel 80 is the tier's helmet 60 plus 20
      for the mechanitor hardware, short of the mechlord's 120 because the shell is the
      chassis's own.

    Art: the only piece with masks (_northm/_eastm/_southm for the worn Graphic_Multi, _m for
    the icon's Graphic_Single), so it draws with CutoutComplex and useWornGraphicMask, as the
    Controller's helmet does. The CompColorable colour paints the mask's red areas and the
    black-masked trim keeps its painted colour (apparel graphics pass white as colorTwo).

    ApparelExtension priority 1, for the reason in the armor's header; Merge still ORs the
    base's isUnifiedApparel and hideHead in.

    Patched by 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml (EVA tag, Insulation_Cold 100), the VGE vacuum patch
    (VGE1's warcasket-helmet VacuumResistance) and the 1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/ root,
    which restates the piece on CE's scale; see their headers.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketHelmetBase">
    <defName>OLWC_WarcasketHelmet_Overlord</defName>
    <label>overlord warcasket helmet</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket helmet with standard protection, equipped with signal enhancers that greatly increase the pilot's mech bandwidth.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket helmet with standard protection, equipped with signal enhancers that greatly increase the pilot's mech bandwidth.\n\nA 10th-generation design from the government program that rebuilt captured pirate rigs around its own power armor and gave them to veterans who could no longer serve any other way. The Overlord was its rig for veteran mechanitors, who would command their own mechs in the field rather than join a squad.\n\nThe Overlord series is meant for a mechanitor who goes into battle alone, with only their mechs beside them. The resurrector in the shell holds a few charges and regains them slowly, so they are best saved for whichever mechs are needed most at the time. The helmet greatly increases the pilot's bandwidth at some cost to their aim, and the shoulders carry command relays that reach mechs anywhere on the map. Because the plating is far tougher than a mechanitor's usual armor, the pilot can lead from the front line rather than from behind the mechs.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/WarcasketOverlordHelmet</texPath>
      <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <uiIconScale>1.25</uiIconScale>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>8</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>10</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>10</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <MechBandwidth>12</MechBandwidth>
      <ShootingAccuracyPawn>-3</ShootingAccuracyPawn>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.1</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.7</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>6</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>80</Plasteel>
      <NanostructuringChip>1</NanostructuringChip>
      <PowerfocusChip>1</PowerfocusChip>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
      <li>UltraMechtech</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>FullHead</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/WarcasketOverlordHelmet</wornGraphicPath>
      <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
      <layers>
        <li>Overhead</li>
      </layers>
    </apparel>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
